<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
        </smile>
        <name>III Simple Non-Linear</name>
        <uuid>54ecbe87-9b50-4bd8-890b-135ade617cfb</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="Minutes" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>60</stop>
        <dt>0.25</dt>
        <isee:analyze_mode>false</isee:analyze_mode>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="model" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" link_high_level_map="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="1334" height="630" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="595" height="744" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="sector" />
    <model>
        <stock name="Heat_Available">
            <doc>This value was chosen to meet the needs of the final model.</doc>
            <eqn>210000&#x0D;{Joules}</eqn>
            <outflow>Heat_Loss</outflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="170" y="137" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Heat_Loss">
            <doc>This is a simple negative feedback structure depicting a situation where a cup with decreasing heat content (decreasing temperature) will lose heat progressively more slowly.  The value of the &quot;.1&quot; cooling coefficient was chosen to allow equilibration in approximately the 1 hour run of the simulation.  A quite valid other approach would be to use a separate converter to hold that definition so that it could be easily changed if needed to explore other scenarios.</doc>
            <eqn>Heat_Available * .1&#x0D;{Joules per minute}</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="265" y="132" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="85">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="190" y="132" />
                    <pt x="340" y="132" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Coffee_Temperature">
            <doc>This is a bit convoluted but it provides an initial energy content of the coffee (104,600 Joules) so that, when divided by the specific heat of water (4.184 Joules/gram * degree centigrade) and the massof 1 cup of coffee (250 grams), the initial temperature is 100 degrees centigrade.</doc>
            <eqn>(Heat_Available - 105400)/(4.184*250)&#x0D;{Degrees centigrade}</eqn>
            <display x="201" y="223" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Room_Temperature">
            <doc>This is the conventional value for room temperature.</doc>
            <eqn>25&#x0D;{degrees centigrade}</eqn>
            <display x="361" y="223" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <display page_width="595" page_height="744" isee:converter_size="large" interval="DT">
            <connector x="163" y="152" uid="0">
                <from>Heat_Available</from>
                <to>Coffee_Temperature</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="190" y="154" uid="1">
                <from>Heat_Available</from>
                <to>Heat_Loss</to>
            </connector>
            <stacked_container x="44" y="284" height="282" width="492" uid="2">
                <graph type="time_series" title="Untitled" background="#C8C8C8" show_grid="true" plot_numbers="true" isee:use_five_segments="false" date_time="2025-02-04T09:45:42Z" cleared="true" time_precision="2" from="0" to="60">
                    <plot index="0" pen_width="1" color="red" precision="0.01" show_y_axis="true">
                        <scale min="-100" max="100" />
                        <entity name="Coffee_Temperature" />
                    </plot>
                    <plot index="1" pen_width="1" color="blue" precision="0.01" show_y_axis="true">
                        <scale min="-100" max="100" />
                        <entity name="Room_Temperature" />
                    </plot>
                </graph>
            </stacked_container>
            <pad_icon x="166" y="439" width="26" height="22" color="fuchsia" label_side="bottom" label="Graph 1" type="graph" icon_of="2" />
            <text_box x="64" y="1" uid="3" color="#7F00FF" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="459" height="61">COOLING COFFEE II&#x0D;Model to Accompany Powers&apos;&#x0D;III.  Non-Linear Heat Loss Due to Decreasing Heat Content&#x0D;</text_box>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        </display>
        <interface page_cols="0" page_rows="0" page_width="1588" page_height="1128" home_page="0">
            <simulation_delay>0</simulation_delay>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        </interface>
        <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </model>
</xmile>
